/P 331 0 R
/E (Few-shot anomaly detection in time-series data focuses on identifying unusual patterns in sequential data such as stock prices, sensor readings, or website traffic. Instead of relying on large amounts of labeled data, few-shot learning enables the system to learn normal behavior from a very small number of examples. This makes it especially useful in real-world situations where anomaly data is rare or difficult to collect. By detecting deviations from normal patterns without requiring extensive labeled datasets, the system can effectively identify potential issues at an early stage. As a result, it plays a crucial role in the early detection of equipment failures, financial fraud, security breaches, and other system faults, helping organizations respond quickly and reduce potential risks.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
